# Variadic param collects excess positional args into a lazy Seq cons-list (at runtime).
# The variadic param type is Seq(T) where T is inferred from the supplied args.
# Grammar forbids @annotation on variadic params. param_types[i] and the env binding
# are both set to Seq(fresh TypeVar) for type inference.
# At runtime, excess positional args are collected into a Seq cons-list.
# Empty variadic = Dict({}) (the nil sentinel); non-empty = Seq(head, ...).
[f: [fn [x ...rest] rest]
 result: [f 10 20 30]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x, rest), "result": Seq(Int(20), ...)})
